{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 67, :comments ["<b>Into the tent of Sarah his mother.</b> He brought her into the tent, and she became the likeness of Sarah his mother — that is, she is now Sarah his mother: for all the days that Sarah was alive, a lamp burned from Sabbath eve to Sabbath eve, and a blessing was found in the dough, and a cloud was bound over the tent; and when she died, these ceased, and when Rebecca came, they returned (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>After his mother.</b> It is the way of the world: all the while that a man's mother is alive, he is bound to her; and once she dies, he is comforted by his wife."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:21.277633745Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}